codex
The derived summary was competing correctly by priority, but the fully symbolic call-frame claim still drives the backend into expensive condition solving around the generic frame machinery. The proof obligation that matters—the arbitrary finite list loop—already closes directly without the summary. I’m narrowing the second claim to a concrete empty-list call-frame check, so it verifies closure entry/parameter binding/return/pop while the first claim remains the universal functional-correctness proof.
